# CC-MC — environment variable reference
#
# This file documents every variable CCMC.Cloud.Api and the local Docker
# Compose setup consume. It is a REFERENCE, not something you run against
# directly - copy one of the environment-specific templates instead:
#
#   .env.local.example       -> copy to .env.local      (local Docker Compose)
#   .env.production.example  -> copy to .env.production (Neon / Render)
#
# Real, secret-bearing files (.env, .env.local, .env.production, ...) are
# gitignored and must NEVER be committed - see .gitignore and README.md
# "Environment Configuration". Only the *.example templates (placeholders
# only) are committed.
#
# The application's configuration binding is unchanged across every
# environment - only these values differ. Names below match exactly what
# CCMC.Cloud.Api/Program.cs reads (ASP.NET Core's double-underscore ->
# nested-config-key convention):

# --- Required by CCMC.Cloud.Api ---------------------------------------------

# Development | Production. Controls Swagger, the DevelopmentSeeder
# (dev-only demo users), and detailed error pages - see appsettings.json's
# own _comment and Program.cs.
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development

# Standard Npgsql keyword connection string. Host is the ONLY thing that
# changes between local Docker (the cc-mc-postgres service/container
# hostname) and Neon (Neon's own hostname) - see .env.local.example /
# .env.production.example.
ConnectionStrings__CcmcDb=Host=REPLACE_ME;Port=5432;Database=REPLACE_ME;Username=REPLACE_ME;Password=REPLACE_ME

# HMAC signing secret for issued JWTs - a long random string, NOT a
# business value, NOT reused between environments. Generate one with e.g.
# `openssl rand -base64 48`.
Jwt__Secret=REPLACE_ME

# --- Optional (CCMC.Cloud.Api falls back to sensible defaults - see
# JwtOptions.cs / Program.cs - only set these if you need non-default
# values) ---
# Jwt__Issuer=ccmc-cloud-api
# Jwt__Audience=ccmc-windows-client

# Render (or any similar PaaS) injects this - CCMC.Cloud.Api honors it if
# present (see Program.cs) and falls back to the base image's own default
# (8080) otherwise. Not needed for local Docker Compose (compose.yaml maps
# a host port to the container's fixed 8080 instead).
# PORT=

# --- Local Docker Compose only (see .env.local.example) --------------------
# POSTGRES_USER=
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_DB=
# API_HOST_PORT=
# POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=

# --- Windows client only (src/CCMC.Desktop/appsettings.json, NOT an env
# var today - listed here for completeness of "what changes per
# environment") ---
# CloudApi:BaseUrl = http://localhost:5000/           (local dev / local Docker)
# CloudApi:BaseUrl = https://<render-api-domain>/      (future, once Render is deployed - NOT set yet)
